            {
              "id": "80ad65b8-c81a-4567-a1c3-56734d7de813",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong><strong>Children and Play in the Holocaust: Games Among the Shadows </strong></strong></em>was written by George Eisen, published by University of Massachusetts Press in 1990."
            },
            {
              "id": "ee7cea56-ae98-4094-b18c-8c0d55602a75",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "7c13ccaf-36bd-45d9-a7a0-d962be72bbbc",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Occasionally an accident of research produces a book more engaging than the one the historian originally intended. While sifting through material for his Ph.D. dissertation, which dealt with an entirely different topic, Eisen came across a diary from the Vilna ghetto written by Zelig Kalmanovitch. His tone was sober, but not entirely so. The passage that caught Eisen’s eye concerned a playground erected around 1942 and the author’s inner conflict surrounded the coexistence of games and sports and mass murder in the ghetto.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "c60f9a82-25bf-451a-b58c-fa8223bcdd76",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
          ]
        },
